  "answer": "The goal was not met. Code confirmed four settings on four different scenes (S1, S3, S7, S9), not the five asked for, and the video triage shows only one of them is clearly a policy error. At S1 (scene 023b7fcc, no time shift, cars at 1.25x speed), the policy drifted left out of its lane and hit a car driving alongside, even though it was told to go straight and the recorded human went right. So the left drift still causes collisions at 2 Hz planning. At S3 and S7, which speed the cars up to 1.5x and 2x, every failure was a replayed car from behind driving through the ego at the moment the policy took over. These are rear-end overlaps that were counted as front collisions, not policy failures, and the plan said to ignore rear-end hits. At S9 a replayed car overtook the ego and cut across into it; the triage could not say whether the policy was at fault. Each confirmed setting rests on only a few repeats, so their failure ranges are wide even though they clear one half.",
